<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wolfgang, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1526">1526</a>–<a href="/years/1569">1569</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wolfgang, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zweibrucken">Zweibrücken</a>, was a Wittelsbach prince who introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in his lands and inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-neuburg">Palatinate-Neuburg</a> in 1557. By the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> in 1543 he ceded Veldenz to his uncle Rupert. He died in 1569 while leading troops to aid the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huguenots">Huguenots</a>, and his lands were divided among his sons, founding several Palatine lines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wolfgang-count-palatine-of-zweibrucken.jpg" alt="Wolfgang, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unbekannter Künstler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wolfgang_von_Zweibr%C3%BCcken-Neuburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
